# Eluge, the Shoreless Sea: "power and toughness are each equal to the number of Islands you control" (CR 604.3) and "Whenever
# Eluge enters or attacks, put a flood counter on target land. It's an Island in addition to its other types for as long as it
# has a flood counter on it" (CR 611.2b, 205.1b). Turn 1 plays an Island, turn 3 a Mountain, and Black Lotus and the Island
# pay for Eluge. It enters as a 1/1 (one Island), its enters trigger floods the Mountain, which is then an Island in addition
# to a Mountain - Eluge 2/2 - and taps for {U} (CR 305.6) as well as {R}. Turn 5 it attacks and floods Bot2's Mountain, which becomes an Island in addition to its types,
# but Eluge counts only the Islands its controller controls: still 3/3 with the third land, not 4/4. Bot2 takes 3. In the second
# main phase Time Walk ({1}{U}), the first instant or sorcery spell of the turn, costs {U} less for the one flooded land Bot1
# controls - not {U}{1} less, which counting Bot2's flooded Mountain would make it - so an Island pays its {1} and no mana is
# left over. Time Walk's extra turn is turn 6; on turn 7 Bot2 controls a flooded land too, but the reduction is only for Eluge's
# controller's spells: Bot2's Lightning Strike costs its full {1}{R}, paid by its two lands with nothing left over.

